KG42.register("clusters-5a3dff64a4674d32c855b9a4",{"id":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v142-d-K005","paper":"11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation","label":"Candidate for BS net energy submission and intertemporal cost and revenue allocation","record":{"cluster_id":"v142-d-K005","label":"Candidate for BS net energy submission and intertemporal cost and revenue allocation","market_meaning":"BS requires continued use of the A18 net energy submission format, with demand and supply bids aggregated across time entering the calculation of internal prices, through which regional costs and revenues are allocated in proportion to quantity. The indices, export numerator, and intertemporal price interpretation in the existing A28 remain insufficient to form a closed settlement rule.","mechanism_ids":["v141-a-M03"],"market_types":["LEM"],"process_stages":["bidding","pricing","settlement"],"scope_disposition":"unresolved","scope_explanation":"Only evidence and chains registered under M03 are referenced, preserving the intertemporal scope of BS without importing SDR pricing by time period or MMR component bids. A18 is only referenced by evidence within the same mechanism, and the mathematics of R019 remains unresolved; the wording of allocation in proportion to quantity and average sharing also cannot be assumed to have the same meaning.","assembly_status":"partial","boundary_rationale":"The submission format, the interface through which bids enter prices, and the intertemporal cost and revenue allocation carried by prices have direct functional relationships; the four chains jointly form a BS allocation candidate, with all existing mathematical questions explicitly retained.","chain_bindings":[{"chain_id":"v141-c-R017","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Retains the format requirement for the BS demand side to continue using A18, without drawing on other mechanisms to supply missing objects."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R018","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Complements the supply-side requirements of the same net energy submission format."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R019","ownership":"primary","role":"interface","rationale":"Provides the existing procedural interface through which demand and supply bids enter BS price calculation; the C2 mathematics that was not adopted is not reinstated."},{"chain_id":"v141-c-R020","ownership":"primary","role":"core","rationale":"Carries the existing A28 and its interpretation of regional cost and revenue allocation, retained as the main mathematical content awaiting clarification."}],"connections":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K005-CN01","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R017","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R018","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R017::phi::v141-c-R017-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R018::phi::v141-c-R018-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"],"rationale":"The same BS evidence requires the use of the A18 format, and the two chains cover the demand and supply sides of net energy respectively; this format requirement is not changed into the MMR requirement for separate submissions."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K005-CN02","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R017","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R019","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R017::phi::v141-c-R017-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R019::phi::v141-c-R019-C002","v141-c-R019::E::v141-c-R019-E001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"],"rationale":"The BS bid-format requirement connects to the procedural interface through which positive net demand enters the intertemporal aggregation for the buying price; because bid quantities are not typed, no completed variable-level identity mapping is claimed."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K005-CN03","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R018","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R019","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R018::phi::v141-c-R018-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R019::phi::v141-c-R019-C001","v141-c-R019::E::v141-c-R019-E002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"],"rationale":"Supply-side net energy submission corresponds to the input description for calculating the selling price; only the input's use is confirmed, without thereby endorsing the net-quantity interpretation of the export numerator in A28."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K005-CN04","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R019","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R020","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R019::phi::v141-c-R019-C001","v141-c-R019::phi::v141-c-R019-C002"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R020::phi::v141-c-R020-C001","v141-c-R020::E::v141-c-R020-E001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08","v141-b-g03-E30"],"rationale":"The source directly links internal prices to the allocation of regional costs and revenues according to consumption and generation quantities, so the price-input description and allocation expression are read jointly; the R020 expression does not backfill or repair the unresolved mathematics of R019."}],"object_mappings":[{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K005-OM01","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R017::V::bidding.demand","v141-c-R019::V::bidding.demand"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R017::V::bidding.demand","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"],"rationale":"All represent the BS net-demand submission function; their associated display is confined to M03, and they are not merged with identically named SDR nodes."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K005-OM02","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R018::V::bidding.supply","v141-c-R019::V::bidding.supply"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R018::V::bidding.supply","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"],"rationale":"The nodes at both locations correspond to the BS supply-bid submission function, retaining all original procedural constraints and edges."},{"mapping_id":"v142-d-K005-OM03","kind":"same_node","member_refs":["v141-c-R019::V::pricing.local","v141-c-R020::V::pricing.local"],"canonical_ref":"v141-c-R019::V::pricing.local","display_policy":"single_representative","evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"],"rationale":"The same BS internal-price function appears in the input interface and the payment-allocation chain; node identity does not mean that the mathematics of the two chains is already consistent or that A28 has been confirmed."}],"gaps":[{"gap_id":"v142-d-K005-G01","category":"unverified_source","description":"A28 and its textual explanation both retain unverified status; this experiment did not conduct B source review, C2 independent review, or Agent E validation.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R017","v141-c-R018","v141-c-R019","v141-c-R020"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R020::phi::v141-c-R020-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08","v141-b-g03-E30"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Independently check all operators, absolute-value placements, indices, and explanations in the original A28, then review this cluster's interfaces."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K005-G02","category":"upstream_missing","description":"The M03 evidence states only that A18 continues to be used, without providing the complete formula or symbol definitions; R017/R018 lack the corresponding bid-quantity objects. The A18 objects from M01 cannot be copied to circumvent the source scope of the same mechanism.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R017","v141-c-R018"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R017::phi::v141-c-R017-C001","v141-c-R018::phi::v141-c-R018-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Add upstream an A18 reference explicitly registered under M03 and the complete source scope, and determine the required objects for bids, device terms, indices, and units; only the format rule is retained at present."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K005-G03","category":"upstream_missing","description":"R019 still contains only procedural constraints, and the C2 candidate that was not adopted cannot be reintroduced through R020; R020 also lacks typed quantity objects for bid inputs and internal prices. Node associations are insufficient to complete these mathematical interfaces.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R019","v141-c-R020"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R019::phi::v141-c-R019-C001","v141-c-R019::phi::v141-c-R019-C002","v141-c-R020::phi::v141-c-R020-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Resolve the mathematics of R019 and the quantity references in R020 through explicit subsequent C revisions; all revisions must preserve source scope, and D neither reinstates candidates nor adds scientific objects in this round."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K005-G04","category":"math_incomplete","description":"T_l^+ and T_l^- in A28 involve participant n, but whether the sets are defined separately for each participant is not specified; there are also no rules for handling empty sets of positive or negative bids or zero denominators.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R019","v141-c-R020"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R020::phi::v141-c-R020-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Check the participant indexing of the time sets, the summation ranges, and the applicability conditions for empty sets; do not automatically add subscripts, default prices, or zero-denominator handling before clarification."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K005-G05","category":"math_incomplete","description":"In periods of regional net export, the existing A28 takes the absolute value of each participant's bid before aggregation, potentially also including demand in that period in the export-revenue numerator; it therefore cannot be directly equated with the regional net export quantity or used to claim conservation of export revenue.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R019","v141-c-R020"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R019::phi::v141-c-R019-C001","v141-c-R020::phi::v141-c-R020-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Recheck the absolute-value placement and net-export interpretation in the original to determine whether this is a transcription issue, an issue in the source, or a matter of another definition; do not independently move the absolute-value signs or replace the numerator."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K005-G06","category":"math_incomplete","description":"A28 places external prices bearing a time-period index outside the intertemporal aggregates, while t is also used for summation; when tariffs vary across time periods, its interpretation of total regional costs and revenues remains unclosed, and evidence within the same mechanism provides no constant-tariff restriction sufficient to resolve the question.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R020"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R020::theta::v141-c-R020-P001","v141-c-R020::theta::v141-c-R020-P002","v141-c-R020::phi::v141-c-R020-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Clarify the temporal applicability of external prices, the free index, and the intertemporal cost interpretation; do not directly import tariff assumptions from other mechanisms or rewrite the expression as a new weighted-cost formula."},{"gap_id":"v142-d-K005-G07","category":"ambiguous_mapping","description":"The BS wording of average sharing coexists with the explanation of allocation in proportion to energy produced and consumed; equal allocation cannot be inferred from this, nor can the difference between the two interpretations be eliminated without checking.","chain_ids":["v141-c-R020"],"object_refs":["v141-c-R020::phi::v141-c-R020-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g07-ev-08","v141-b-g07-ev-09","v141-b-g03-E30","v141-b-g05-E08"],"proposal_ids":[],"required_work":"Use A28 together with the discussion of the same mechanism to clarify whether average sharing means uniform allocation across time or equal allocation among participants; at present, do not generate a second allocation rule or select one interpretation to replace the original explanation."}]},"rule_refs":["11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R017","11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R018","11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R019","11-p2p_mechanisms_evaluation::v141-c-R020"],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"node_ids":["COMP-2a46795d52ce8b8d","COMP-3ec89227e9cd067c","COMP-c0cbb067ee5d581a","COMP-f276c683eb055d9b"]});
